Offline Evals Vs Online Evals | CampusX

offline evals are the ones which will come into picture before deployment 

what are the main purpose of offline evals.
1) Pre-release testing (I can properly test my application before deployment)
2) Version comparison (evaluate open ai model vs claude model which is better for me based on the same golden datasets)
we can compare different models, prompts, re-rankers,vector dbs etc.
3) Regression testing

but What about Post Deployment
1) Un-anticipated Inputs - questions mixing Hindi and English,ambiguous half questions, angry rants with real questions buried inside, adversarial prompt injections attempts, questions about edge cases scenarios you never considered earlier in offline Evals.

2) Emergent / systematic failures -  problems that only exist at scale, under load, over time. (A retrieval index silently lagging its source document, cost per conversation quietly tripling after a prompt change, the latency tail (p99) frustrating a slice of users, a subtle bias that only becomes visible across thousands of conversations, degradation that only appears under real concurrent load.)

3) Drift -  offline eval gets obselete.

Online Evals - Its evaluating your system on live production traffic, after deployment, as real users interact with it.


🟦 = OFFLINE EVAL (before deployment)      🟨 = ONLINE EVAL (after deployment)

+--------------+-----------------------------------+----------------------------------------+
|              | 🟦 OFFLINE EVAL                   | 🟨 ONLINE EVAL                         |
|              | 🟦 (before deployment)            | 🟨 (after deployment)                  |
+--------------+-----------------------------------+----------------------------------------+
| Data         | 🟦 Fixed, pre-collected dataset   | 🟨 Live production traffic             |
| Answer key   | 🟦 Known in advance               | 🟨 None - must estimate quality        |
| Timing       | 🟦 Runs before shipping           | 🟨 Runs continuously, live             |
| Inputs seen  | 🟦 Only what you anticipated      | 🟨 The real, messy distribution        |
| Catches      | 🟦 Known regressions              | 🟨 Drift, surprises, emergent bugs     |
| Best for     | 🟦 Gating, version comparison, CI | 🟨 Real-world quality, drift detection |
+--------------+-----------------------------------+----------------------------------------+
Biggest Challenge - In production, there is no answer key. 

offline evals- is your application functioning correctly?
online evals - is you application working normally in production?

Online Eval pipeline - important part is logging.. whatever is happening in production

Logging
Capture a structured, replayable of every conversation turn.

Logging  --> Sampling  --> evaluator --> Dashbaord --> Alerts

🟪 = COMPUTED (produced by an evaluator)      🟩 = CAPTURED (read directly from trace)

+-----------------------------------+-------------------------------------+
| 🟪 COMPUTED                       | 🟩 CAPTURED                         |
| 🟪 (produced by an evaluator)     | 🟩 (read directly from trace)       |
+-----------------------------------+-------------------------------------+
| 🟪 Faithfulness                   | 🟩 Thumbs up / down                 |
| 🟪 Answer relevance               | 🟩 Escalation rate                  |
| 🟪 Correctness                    | 🟩 Abandonment / drop-off           |
| 🟪 Hallucination                  | 🟩 Rephrase rate                    |
| 🟪 Toxicity                       | 🟩 Conversion                       |
| 🟪 Bias & fairness                | 🟩 Latency (p50 / p95 / p99)        |
| 🟪 PII leakage / prompt injection | 🟩 Cost per conversation            |
| 🟪 Conciseness                    | 🟩 Token usage                      |
| 🟪 Task completion, satisfaction  | 🟩 Error rate                       |
+-----------------------------------+-------------------------------------+
if there is a evaluator on the tracing.. then its a online evaluator..
if there is a evaluator on the datasets.. then its a offline evaluator.
Langsmith is a online+offline evaluation platform.





